From fc8e5322bebae902cdf39f26125661e4ec47d942 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "suricata.lu" <suricata.lu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:50:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tools/virtio: Make compiler-context-analysis.h visible to the
 tools build

Patch 0622 in the v6.12.112-cip33 folder, the stable backport of upstream
commit de15fecae44d ("compiler_types: Move lock checking attributes to
compiler-context-analysis.h"), makes include/linux/compiler_types.h
include <linux/compiler-context-analysis.h>. tools/virtio uses the
kernel's compiler_types.h directly (see tools/virtio/linux/compiler.h),
but the new header is not in its include path, so the tools no longer
build:

  fatal error: linux/compiler-context-analysis.h: No such file or directory

The kernel-tools recipe in meta-imx builds virtio-ivshmem-console and
virtio-ivshmem-block from tools/virtio, so the image build fails.

Add tools/virtio/linux/compiler-context-analysis.h that includes the
kernel's header, in the same way tools/virtio/linux/compiler.h includes
compiler_types.h. The macros get the same definitions as before 0622.

Upstream fixed the tools build differently in 944e3f7562c5 ("tools:
Update context analysis macros in compiler_types.h"), which adds a stub
header to tools/include and removes the old macros from
tools/include/linux/compiler_types.h. That change is not in 6.12 stable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/virtio/linux/compiler-context-analysis.h | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tools/virtio/linux/compiler-context-analysis.h

diff --git a/tools/virtio/linux/compiler-context-analysis.h b/tools/virtio/linux/compiler-context-analysis.h
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..8a49abf38fb7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/virtio/linux/compiler-context-analysis.h
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 */
+#ifndef LINUX_COMPILER_CONTEXT_ANALYSIS_H
+#define LINUX_COMPILER_CONTEXT_ANALYSIS_H
+
+#include "../../../include/linux/compiler-context-analysis.h"
+
+#endif
